# Phase <PHASE> Spec — Covenant + Invariants

Flavor: `<FLAVOR>`

Read once at phase start. Re-read on `/compact` recovery.

## Per-task covenant

### Positive (every task does this)

- exactly one commit per task
- title only; no commit body unless the "why" is non-obvious
- format: `type(scope): subject (P<PHASE>-Bxx)`
- types: `feat` / `fix` / `test` / `chore` / `docs` / `refactor` / `perf` / `build` / `ci`
- scopes: <list project units here — e.g. packages in a monorepo (`uikit`, `docs`), services in a polyrepo (`api`, `worker`, `web`), modules in a library (`auth`, `db`, `core`), or surfaces (`migration`, `infra`, `cli`)>
- subject in imperative mood, ≤ 50 chars
- sibling test in `git diff` (TDD gate enforced — see `references/HOOK-RESPONSES.md`)
- rebaselined goldens included in the same commit when output changes (see `references/OUTPUT-REBASELINE.md`)
- meta-gate updates in same commit when applicable (see `references/META-GATE.md`)

### Negative (no task ever does this)

- never `git add -A` or `git add .` — explicit paths only
- never `--no-verify` / `--no-gpg-sign`
- never `git commit --amend` after publish
- never HEREDOC in `git commit -m "..."`
- never backticks in commit messages (PreToolUse pattern matches command substitution)
- never `git reset --hard` on tracked changes
- never `git push` (user owns push)
- never `gh pr create` (user owns PR)
- never `npm publish` / `changeset publish` / `cargo publish` / `terraform apply` / `kubectl apply` / `dbt run` against prod (user owns release / deploy / apply)
- never use `.changeset/` for dossier internals — closeout stays under `.scratchpad/dossier/closeout/`
- never edit `.env` files (read-blocked + write-blocked)
- never co-author lines (disabled in user settings anyway)
- never touch parallel-session work — multiple sessions may run; never revert / checkout / discard without confirmation

## Invariants (R-rules)

These hold across the phase. If a task would violate one, file a
new finding in `AUDIT.md` instead.

Stack-neutral floor (always on):

- **R1** — every changed unit has at least one sibling test in the same commit (TDD gate)
- **R2** — flaky single test: skip + file a finding, never raise project-wide retry count
- **R3** — long-running command (>30s wall): use the selected runtime adapter, never `sleep` in shell
- **R4** — formatter reformats after Edit/Write: `Read` again before next Edit on the same file
- **R5** — TDD gate blocks impl edit without sibling test in `git diff`: write the test first
- **R6** — meta-gate test counts as the sibling for config / threshold / structural files (see `references/META-GATE.md`)
- **R7** — output rebaseline never runs before the unbaselined diff is read (see `references/OUTPUT-REBASELINE.md`)

Phase-specific (fill in for this phase):

- **R8** — <invariant: e.g. "all public exports listed in `api-surface.json`">
- **R9** — <invariant: e.g. "all DB migrations linear, no merge conflicts on serial">
- **R10** — <invariant: e.g. "all CLI commands have exit-code matrix in fixtures">

